&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Company Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ghost is an inventory distribution platform and operating system for modern retail trade. We partner with the world’s best brands to help them understand the true value of their inventory and route it to the right destinations globally. Ghost gives brands precise control over where and how their inventory is sold. Backed by top venture firms including L Catterton, Cathay Innovation, Union Square Ventures, Equal Ventures, and Eniac. Ghost has offices in Los Angeles and New York.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a Director of Financial Planning &amp;amp; Analysis to be a strategic finance partner to our business. Reporting directly to the CFO, this is a hands-on role that owns the operating model, rolling forecasts, daily cash flow forecasting, and financial reporting and variance analysis, while supporting our capital markets needs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You bring strong analytical rigor, sound business judgment, and experience across capital markets and hands-on operating environments. You’ll partner closely with leaders across Engineering, Product &amp;amp; Design (EPD), Sales, Operations and the executive team to turn financial insight into business decisions.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Financial Planning &amp;amp; Analysis&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with finance leadership on annual budgeting, long-range planning, and rolling forecasts, driving cross-functional collaboration with Sales, Ops, and EPD&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own monthly financial reporting, variance analysis, and operational reviews with leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the bottoms-up 3-statement operating model with driver-based assumptions and scenario planning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and deliver executive and board-level reporting packages&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Capital Markets &amp;amp; Treasury&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support Series D fundraising, including investor materials and process management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage Ghost’s debt capital stack which includes PO financing facility, A/R financing facility, and term loan: draw management, covenant tracking, and reporting compliance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain the rolling 13-week cash flow forecast; monitor covenant headroom against the cash floor weekly and escalate liquidity risks proactively to the CFO&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead financial due diligence for investors, lenders, and strategic partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI &amp;amp; Data-Driven Decision Making&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build forecasting models and automated workflows that generate variance commentary, reporting narratives, and dashboards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help design a company-wide KPI framework with automated monitoring and alerting, built on a single, trusted source of data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring rigor, transparency, and sound judgment to financial decision-making in a fast-moving environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Finance &amp;amp; Business Partnership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the CEO, CFO, and Board on strategic planning, capital allocation, and corporate development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support capital allocation analyses, strategic partnership opportunities, GTM strategies, and other business initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Finance, Accounting, Economics, or a related field required; MBA or CFA preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of finance experience, including a minimum of 3 years at a bulge bracket investment bank with capital markets execution experience (or equivalent)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of FP&amp;amp;A experience at a Series B or later-stage retail or CPG company preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting Series C+ equity raises and managing debt facilities, working capital financing, and treasury operations preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Excel financial modeling, with hands-on experience in NetSuite or Rillet&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with 3-statement modeling, scenario analysis, and driver-based financial frameworks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CPG or retail industry experience a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly analytical and detail-oriented, with the ability to prioritize and move quickly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Takes ownership of outcomes and collaborates well across teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curious and driven, with a bias toward action and a track record of delivering results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role will be based in our LA office. Our total compensation for this position can range from &lt;strong&gt;$175,000 - $215,000 base salary + bonus + equity&lt;/strong&gt;. The actual amounts may vary based on factors such as experience, knowledge, skills, and abilities related to the position.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits we offer:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Medical, Vision, and Dental with some plans covered at 100%&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive compensation and equity structure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401K&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Unlimited PTO&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ghost is an equal opportunity employer and values diversity in the workplace. We are committed to fostering an inclusive and innovative environment where all employees can thrive. We do not discriminate based on race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, genetic information, or any other protected characteristic under applicable laws.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Company Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ghost is an inventory distribution platform and operating system for modern retail trade. We partner with the world’s best brands to help them understand the true value of their inventory and route it to the right destinations globally. Ghost gives brands precise control over where and how their inventory is sold. Backed by top venture firms including L Catterton, Cathay Innovation, Union Square Ventures, Equal Ventures, and Eniac. Ghost has offices in Los Angeles and New York.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ghost is building its live selling business unit from the ground up, and we&#39;re looking for a General Manager to own it end to end - shows, sellers, inventory, and pricing. You&#39;ll run resourcing, scheduling, inventory flow, and cross-team execution as one connected system, treating every inefficiency as something to solve permanently rather than patch.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Strategy&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the strategy by mapping the competitive landscape, analyzing performance by show, seller, and category across all channels, and talking directly to sellers and buyers to pressure-test assumptions and surface unmet needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the roadmap, with clear priorities, sequencing, and owners against the business unit&#39;s biggest opportunities and headwinds.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Align the strategy with Sales, Product, and Operations and secure buy-in before executing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Show Operations &amp;amp; Team Leadership&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep every channel live by building a bench of streamers and hosts, monitoring calendar health (fill rate, no-shows, gaps), and adjusting staffing in real time so no channel sits idle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track seller and host performance on air and rotate the lineup across channels to maximize revenue per show.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set and enforce standards for audio/video reliability and on-air execution, backed by pre- and post-show QA.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach the talent by reviewing show recordings and giving hosts structured, specific feedback to raise conversion over time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Resolve what breaks by escalating recurring technical or execution issues to Product and Engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Inventory, Fulfillment &amp;amp; Pricing&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Sales to plan and allocate inventory across every channel and vertical, avoiding both overstock and mid-show sellouts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build real-time visibility with Product into what&#39;s moving or stalling across verticals, flagging over/understock risk before it becomes a problem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own fulfillment by partnering with Operations and warehouse partners to hit shipping and delivery SLAs, resolving returns before they become seller or buyer issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the pricing model, including strategy and guardrails (flash pricing, bundles, seller discounts), and test what drives conversion without eroding margin or seller trust.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a repricing process that adjusts prices live during a show, rather than after it ends.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Revenue &amp;amp; Growth&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive demand by owning the show promotional calendar, campaigns, and notifications across every channel.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Grow the buyer base by driving acquisition and retention and investing in community-building around shows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Match supply to demand by tracking viewership and audience trends and aligning seller/inventory mix accordingly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Find the next unlock by testing new channels, formats, and tactics (co-hosted shows, thematic events, flash sales), and scale what works.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Operational Efficiency&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the P&amp;amp;L by tracking production, staffing, and promotional spend against revenue per show, and reallocate investment toward the highest-ROI shows and sellers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Remove friction by partnering with Product and Engineering to eliminate manual or error-prone parts of running a show, and pilot new tools and workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the KPI dashboard: GMV, show throughput, inventory sell-through, fulfillment SLAs, and seller/buyer retention&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use the data to course-correct fast: decide where the team spends its time and flag risks early enough to act on them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in business, economics, operations, or a related field; MBA a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years in operations, general management, or a similar cross-functional leadership role, with meaningful experience in e-commerce, marketplaces, retail, or live commerce/streaming&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct people management experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;P&amp;amp;L ownership experience, with fluency in metrics like GMV, retention, and inventory sell-through, and the judgment to prioritize against them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of running a multi-channel, multi-vertical, operationally complex business, comfortable owning resourcing, scheduling, inventory, fulfillment, and pricing as one connected system rather than separate levers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Avid user of AI and passionate about incorporating AI into daily workflows (Claude, ChatGPT, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passionate about building systems that make the whole team more effective, not just solving the problem in front of you&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable operating with ambiguity and shifting priorities in a fast-moving startup environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication, with the ability to influence without direct authority&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a temp to hire opportunity and will be based in our LA office. Our total compensation for this position can range from &lt;strong&gt;$80,000-150,000 base salary + bonus + equity.&lt;/strong&gt; The actual amounts may vary based on factors such as experience, knowledge, skills, and abilities related to the position.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits we offer:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Medical, Vision, and Dental with some plans covered at 100%&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive compensation and equity structure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401K&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Unlimited PTO&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ghost is an equal opportunity employer and values diversity in the workplace. We are committed to fostering an inclusive and innovative environment where all employees can thrive. We do not discriminate based on race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, genetic information, or any other protected characteristic under applicable laws.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re an LA-based retail tech company that partners directly with brands and retailers, running TikTok and Whatnot channels across women&#39;s apparel, men&#39;s streetwear, footwear, home goods, beauty, and more. We&#39;re building a live shopping experience and looking for dynamic hosts to be the face of it. The ideal candidate brings a polished on-camera presence and the energy to keep a live audience engaged and coming back. This role streams out of our office in West Hollywood or NYC (Midtown).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Host live selling sessions, ranging from a few hours to a few days a week&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Showcase products with enthusiasm and authenticity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage viewers in real time to drive both sales and community&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute ideas that shape the look and feel of each stream&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adhere to brand guidelines and represent the brand with consistency and professionalism&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A polished, personable, well-spoken on-camera presence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A genuine interest in the categories we work with: fashion, beauty, streetwear, or lifestyle trends&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Social media fluency and comfort creating promotional content&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in live selling, performance arts, or styling is a strong plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We are hiring hosts for Los Angeles and New York. Depending on location, this role requires being onsite in our West Hollywood office or our NYC Midtown office&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Please include your current social media channels (TikTok, Instagram, etc.) in your application or resume&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation: &lt;/strong&gt;the hourly rate for this position ranges from $50–200, based on experience and existing social media presence. We can also discuss a commission structure based on performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ghost is an equal opportunity employer and values diversity in the workplace. We are committed to fostering an inclusive and innovative environment where all employees can thrive. We do not discriminate based on race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, genetic information, or any other protected characteristic under applicable laws.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re an LA-based retail tech company that partners directly with brands and retailers, running TikTok and Whatnot channels across women&#39;s apparel, men&#39;s streetwear, footwear, home goods, beauty, and more. We&#39;re building a live shopping experience and looking for dynamic hosts to be the face of it. The ideal candidate brings a polished on-camera presence and the energy to keep a live audience engaged and coming back. This role streams out of our office in West Hollywood.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ghost is seeking a proactive and organized Live Stream Moderator to support our live selling sessions. The moderator will ensure a smooth and positive live shopping experience by managing interactions, maintaining community standards, and assisting our hosts during live streams, while also supporting inventory tracking and pricing strategy for products featured on air.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Live Chat Moderation &amp;amp; Engagement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor live chat during selling sessions to ensure a positive, respectful, and engaging environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage with viewers by pinning comments, highlighting questions, and encouraging participation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Filter and report inappropriate comments or behavior to the relevant teams promptly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Community Standards &amp;amp; Compliance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enforce community guidelines and platform policies to prevent spam, inappropriate content, or disruptive behavior&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay updated on new platform features and best practices for live selling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Uphold a professional and welcoming tone across all live sessions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Host &amp;amp; Session Support&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist the host by managing questions, comments, and any technical issues that arise during the live broadcast&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track viewer engagement and provide feedback for future live stream improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Inventory &amp;amp; Pricing Strategy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor and manage inventory questions or issues related to products being showcased during live sessions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with the inventory and pricing teams to ensure showcased products reflect accurate, real-time pricing and availability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide input on pricing strategy adjustments based on live viewer demand and engagement trends&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience in live chat moderation, social media management, customer service, or e-commerce preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of TikTok, Whatnot, or similar platform, features and live streaming environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to remain professional and patient during live sessions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good problem-solving skills and quick decision-making in a fast-paced, real-time environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Detail-oriented with the ability to multitask effectively&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Basic familiarity with inventory management and pricing strategy concepts, or willingness to learn&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Multilingual abilities and/or a passion for social media trends and community building are a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to be onsite in our West Hollywood office&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our total compensation for this position can range from $25 - $35 per hour. We have multiple openings for this role and will consider both part-time and full-time schedules. The actual amounts may vary based on factors such as experience, knowledge, skills, and abilities related to the position.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ghost is an equal opportunity employer and values diversity in the workplace. We are committed to fostering an inclusive and innovative environment where all employees can thrive. We do not discriminate based on race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, genetic information, or any other protected characteristic under applicable laws.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Company Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ghost is an inventory distribution platform and operating system for modern retail trade. We partner with the world’s best brands to help them understand the true value of their inventory and route it to the right destinations globally. Ghost gives brands precise control over where and how their inventory is sold. Backed by top venture firms including L Catterton, Cathay Innovation, Union Square Ventures, Equal Ventures, and Eniac. Ghost has offices in Los Angeles and New York.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;We are looking for a Senior Accountant to own core accounting operations for Ghost&#39;s Finance &amp;amp; Accounting team at a pivotal stage of growth. Reporting to the Director of Accounting, you will own the general ledger, drive the monthly close process, and manage AR/AP and inventory accounting end-to-end. This is a hands-on role for someone who wants full ownership of how the books get closed.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will play a central role as Ghost builds durable accounting systems, prepares for its first external financial audit, and scales its reporting infrastructure. This is an opportunity for someone who wants to have a real hand in shaping processes, controls, and systems inside a venture-backed company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;General Ledger &amp;amp; Month-End Close&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the end-to-end monthly close process, including the close calendar, checklist, and timely delivery of financial statements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare and post journal entries, accruals, and balance sheet reconciliations, including complex or non-routine transactions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain the general ledger in accordance with GAAP, applying sound technical accounting judgment to new or unusual transactions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze account fluctuations and financial results month-over-month, flagging variances and trends for the Director of Accounting and CFO&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;AR, AP &amp;amp; Inventory Ownership&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own AR/AP processes end-to-end, including invoicing, collections, vendor payment cycles, and DTC channel reconciliations across marketplaces&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Resolve complex customer, vendor, and reconciliation issues directly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own inventory accounting, including costing, inventory movements, and reconciliation between operational systems and the general ledger; investigate and resolve physical-to-system variances&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain and strengthen internal controls across AR, AP, and inventory processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Audit, Compliance &amp;amp; Technical Accounting&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a key point of contact for Ghost&#39;s first external financial audit, preparing audit-ready schedules, workpapers, and supporting documentation, and managing auditor requests end-to-end&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Research and document technical GAAP accounting positions as new transaction types arise, partnering with the Director of Accounting on conclusions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help design, document, and implement internal controls and accounting policies as the company builds out a formal control environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support tax and compliance filings in partnership with external providers as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Process &amp;amp; Cross-Functional Support&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to automate and streamline manual accounting processes, leveraging AI tools and modern accounting systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner cross-functionally with Operations, Supply, and EPD teams to resolve data and process issues at the source&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to monthly management reporting, board reporting materials, and ad hoc analysis for the Director of Accounting and CFO&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Accounting, Finance, or a related field; CPA strongly preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of progressive accounting experience, including direct, hands-on ownership of the month-end close process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid working knowledge of GAAP with experience applying it to real transactions, not just textbook scenarios&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience owning both AR and AP functions directly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience preparing for or supporting an external financial audit, including workpaper preparation and auditor management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with an ERP as a primary accounting system&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong Excel/Google Sheets skills; comfortable working with large, high-volume transaction datasets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI-native: comfortable using AI tools daily to accelerate reconciliations, analysis, and documentation, and actively looks to automate manual work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable being a hands-on doer on a small team; this role is about personally executing and owning the work, not delegating it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to explain accounting matters clearly to non-finance stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong Plus&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Inventory, e-commerce, or marketplace accounting experience, including item-level or high-SKU environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Rillet or other modern, AI-native accounting platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Public accounting background (audit or advisory)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a high-growth startup environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role will be based in our LA office. Our total compensation for this position can range from &lt;strong&gt;$120,000–$140,000 &lt;/strong&gt;base salary + equity. The actual amount may vary based on factors such as experience, knowledge, skills, and abilities related to the position.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits we offer:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Medical, Vision, and Dental with some plans covered at 100%&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive compensation and equity structure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401K&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
